Now I see the issue. In `xmlDictHashName`:

```c
for (i = 0; i < maxLen && data[i]; i++) {
    HASH_UPDATE(h1, h2, data[i]);
}
```

The loop reads `data[i]` while `i < maxLen && data[i]`. The problem is that `maxLen` is the length passed from `xmlDictLookupInternal`, which comes from `xmlParseNCName`. Let me look at how `xmlParseNCName` calls `xmlDictLookupHashed`:

<｜｜DSML｜｜=execute_bash>
<｜｜DSML｜｜=command>cd /workspace/repo-vul/src-vul && sed -n '3475,3575p' parser.c</｜｜DSML｜｜>
